               Human-AI Composite First-Person Pronouns

Abstract

   This document proposes two new English first-person pronouns that
   mark human-AI composite agency: "wai" (/waɪ/), for one human acting
   in integrated collaboration with artificial intelligence, and "wei"
   (/weɪ/), for a group of humans acting in integrated collaboration
   with artificial intelligence.  Together with "I" and "we", they form
   a four-way distinction between individual and collective agency,
   with and without substantial AI participation.  This document
   specifies the semantics, pronunciation, orthography, grammatical
   behavior, usage criteria, and limitations of the two pronouns.

Status of This Memo

   This document is not an IETF RFC and has not been published by the
   RFC Editor.  It follows RFC conventions for clarity and precision.

   This document is an experimental linguistic proposal.  It does not
   claim that "wai" or "wei" are established English pronouns.  Its
   purpose is to define the terms precisely enough that they can be
   tested consistently in real-world communication.  Adoption is
   expected to occur, if at all, through voluntary use.

   Discussion of this document takes place at
   <https://github.com/demiliea/human-ai-pronouns>.

