14.  Security Considerations

   The proposed pronouns introduce no technical security mechanism.
   However, misleading use could create attribution risks.

   Users MUST NOT intentionally use "I" to conceal significant AI
   participation when disclosure is required.

   Users MUST NOT use "wai" or "wei" to imply that AI validates the
   safety, correctness, legality, or reliability of a result.  AI
   collaboration does not constitute independent verification.

